[{"text":"PauliReduce is an option for PauliTrick and other functions. It specifies whether a chain of Pauli matrices should be reduced to at most one matrix by rewriting every pair of matrices in terms of commutator and anticommutator.","anchor":"paulireduce"},{"text":"Overview, PauliTrick, PauliSimplify.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"CSI[i, j, k] PauliSimplify[%]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{\\sigma }^i.\\overline{\\sigma }^j.\\overline{\\sigma }^k\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{\\sigma }^i.\\overline{\\sigma }^j.\\overline{\\sigma }^k\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CSI[i, j, k] PauliSimplify[%, PauliReduce -> True]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{\\sigma }^i.\\overline{\\sigma }^j.\\overline{\\sigma }^k\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{\\sigma }^i \\bar{\\delta }^{jk}-\\overline{\\sigma }^j \\bar{\\delta }^{ik}+\\overline{\\sigma }^k \\bar{\\delta }^{ij}+i \\bar{\\epsilon }^{ijk}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"}]